a) nominal height of 80 mm or over;

b) surfaces of the webs are continued by fillets to the inside faces of the flange;

c) flanges are generally symmetrical and of equal width (see also 1.4.7.4.5);

d) outside faces of the flanges are parallel;

e) flanges are either of decreasing thickness from the web to the edge (“tapered flanged”) or of uniform

thickness (“parallel flanged”). Note 3 to entry: A distinction is made between

a) parent sections: sections with web and flange thickness considered as standard,

b) thin sections: sections manufactured with the same series of rolls used in producing the corresponding

parent section, which provides a thinner web or flanges or both (as a result of adjustment of the vertical or horizontal rolls) for an approximately equal nominal height, and

c) thick sections: sections manufactured with the same series of rolls used in producing the corresponding

